    "tactics": "The Giant Turtle is not an aggressive predator. It bites when threatened or when something comes within reach of its neck, and it holds on. Most encounters begin because a party disturbed it. It does not pursue beyond its immediate territory and breaks off if left alone.\n---",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Bite [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 4 + Melee Combat 4), Reach 10 ft. (Large creature, long neck).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 14 damage (6 + 8 Str).</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 14 damage, DR halved (round up).</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Amphibious: The Giant Turtle breathes air and water freely. Shell Defense: The Giant Turtle's DR is 8 against all physical ### Attacks while upright. While Prone, its belly is exposed and DR drops to 3 against all damage types. Stable: Whenever the Giant Turtle would gain the Prone condition, it makes a Fortitude [Easy] save before the condition applies. On success, the condition is avoided entirely. On failure, the turtle is upside down and cannot right itself without effort.To stand, it must succeed on an Acrobatics [Hard] check and spend its full movement that turn. Crushing Bite: On Margin 2, the target is Grappled in addition to taking damage. While Grappled this way the turtle can maintain the hold without further attack rolls; the target makes an opposed Athletics or Acrobatics check against the Turtle's Might 5 + Str 6 to escape.</p>",
